∇ (out map)←allow AnonymiseText raw;student;inst;real;fake;leaks;unk;err
 ⍝ Replace the student's and instructors' names in raw paste raw.
 ⍝ Signals unless every check passes. map: real names ,[1.5] fake names.
  student←StudentName raw
 ⍝ Names as the reference model reads them, plus any uwsch finds (it may be buggy)
  inst←∪(Instructors RefParse raw),{0::⍬ ⋄ Instructors⊃##.uwsch ⍵}raw
  real←(⊂student),inst
  fake←(⊂FakeStudent),FakeNames inst
  out←(real fake)Replace raw
  err←⍬
 ⍝ 1. No name, or any part of one, is left anywhere
  :If 0<≢leaks←real Leaks out
      err,←⊂'names still present: ',Quote leaks
  :EndIf
 ⍝ 2. Only the names changed: swapping back gives the original, byte for byte
  :If raw≢(fake real)Replace out
      err,←⊂'swapping names back does not restore the original (a fake name may clash with other text)'
  :EndIf
 ⍝ 3. The same schedule, apart from names, for both the reference model and uwsch
 ⍝    (an error counts as a result: if uwsch fails on the paste it must fail the same way)
  :If ((real fake)Replace RefDump raw)≢RefDump out
  :OrIf ((real fake)Replace SafeDump raw)≢SafeDump out
      err,←⊂'anonymising changed the parsed schedule'
  :EndIf
 ⍝ 4. Nothing we don't recognise, which could be personal data the parser doesn't know about
  :If 0<≢unk←(Unrecognised out)~allow
      err,←⊂'unrecognised text ',(Quote unk),'. If it is not personal data, pass it in the left argument to allow it'
  :EndIf
  :If 0<≢err
      ('Not anonymised: ',⊃{⍺,'; ',⍵}/err)⎕SIGNAL 11
  :EndIf
  map←real,[1.5]fake
∇
